# Feature name: SCATTER_TO_RECT_RATIO
# Feature description: Ratio of SCATTER_RATIO (inertia about minor/major axis) to PR.AXIS_RECTANGULARITY (areaiproportioned to pr.axis dimensions). 
# This feature highlights how the distribution of inertia relates to dimensional proportionality of the vehicle’s silhouette.
# Usefulness: Vehicles like VANs and BUSES, being more rectangular in shape, may exhibit a different scatter-to-rectangularity ratio compared to compact shapes like OPEL or SAAB. This can help the model differentiate between broader and elongated vehicles.
df['SCATTER_TO_RECT_RATIO'] = df['SCATTER_RATIO'] / df['PR.AXIS_RECTANGULARITY']
end

python
# Step 2: Add a new feature for the combined elongation effect
# Feature name: ELONGATION_EFFECT
# Feature description: Combines ELONGATEDNESS and PR.AXIS_ASPECT_RATIO to capture the effect of elongation in both area and axis terms.
# Usefulness: Different vehicle types will have varying aerodynamic and size profiles, which can lead to unique relationships between elongation and axis aspect ratios. This combination can help capture composite features for better classification.
df['ELONGATION_EFFECT'] = df['ELONGATEDNESS'] * df['PR.AXIS_ASPECT_RATIO']
end

python
# Step 3: Add log-transformed features for highly skewed variables
# Feature name: LOG_SCALED_VARIANCE_ALONG_MAJOR_AXIS and LOG_SCALED_VARIANCE_ALONG_MINOR_AXIS
# Feature description: Log transforms of SCALED_VARIANCE_ALONG_MAJOR_AXIS and SCALED_VARIANCE_ALONG_MINOR_AXIS to reduce the impact of large values and normalize their distributions.
